  "notes": "USAGE:\nThe kanji {逸|そ}れる is common in print, but the word is also frequently written in hiragana. The transitive counterpart is {逸|そ}らす (to divert, to deflect).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {話|はなし}が{逸|そ}れる (the conversation goes off track)\n- コースから{逸|そ}れる (to deviate from a course)\n- {的|まと}から{逸|そ}れる (to miss the mark)\n- {本題|ほんだい}から{逸|そ}れる (to stray from the main topic)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {外|はず}れる: to miss, to be off — broader usage, also means \"to be wrong\"\n- ずれる: to shift, to be off — for slight misalignment or discrepancy",
